`Ongoing - Each Player` does not automatically repeat the actions every frame. A rule runs when its conditions become true; if the button stays held, the condition stays true, so completing the action list does not trigger it again. Add a wait and an explicit loop.

```text
variables
{
    player:
        0: Ticks
}

rule("Count while Interact is held")
{
    event
    {
        Ongoing - Each Player;
        All;
        All;
    }

    conditions
    {
        Is Button Held(Event Player, Button(Interact)) == True;
    }

    actions
    {
        Modify Player Variable(Event Player, Ticks, Add, 1);
        Wait(0.100, Abort When False);
        Loop If Condition Is True;
    }
}
```

This increments immediately on pressing Interact, then once every 0.1 seconds while it remains held. `Wait` spaces out the increments. `Abort When False` stops the running action list if the rule condition becomes false during the wait, and `Loop If Condition Is True` returns to the first action only while the condition still holds. Releasing stops the loop; pressing again starts it again. `Ticks` is a player variable, so each player's count is independent and persists between presses.

This example has not been imported into Workshop or tested in-game.
